.TH smi-create-vhost "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-create-vhost \- Create an nginx virtual host configuration from the example template
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-create-vhost
.I DOMAIN BRAND APPS
.br
.B smi-create-vhost
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-create-vhost
copies
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/vhosts/example.com_conf
to
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/vhosts/DOMAIN.conf
in the same directory, replaces the example name with
.IR DOMAIN ,
and comments out the
.B include
line of whichever of brand and apps was switched off.
The file is written mode
.B 0644
and an existing one is never overwritten.
.PP
The template is the one of the nginx configuration itself: two
.B server
blocks, plain HTTP and HTTPS, which include the shared files under
.IR /etc/nginx/commons/server/ .
Writing into
.I /etc/nginx
needs root.
.PP
Without arguments, or with
.BR \-h ,
.B \-\-help
or
.BR help ,
the usage is printed and the command exits 0.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DOMAIN
DNS name to serve, for example
.BR customer.com .
It is lowercased, must be a valid domain name of at most 253 characters, and becomes the
.B server_name
of both blocks and the file name.
.TP
.I BRAND
Whether the brand page is served at
.BR / .
.BR true ,
.BR false ,
.BR yes ,
.BR no ,
.BR y ,
.BR n ,
.BR on ,
.BR off ,
.B 1
or
.BR 0 ,
in any case.
.TP
.I APPS
Whether the applications are served at
.BI /apps/ APP /\fR,
the same values.
Both off is refused, because the virtual host would serve nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was written, or the usage was printed.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong argument count, an invalid domain or switch value, both switches off, a missing vhosts
directory or template, or the target file exists already.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Brand page and applications:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-create-vhost customer.com yes yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only the applications, then reload nginx:
.RS
.nf
sudo smi-create-vhost apps.customer.com no yes
sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/vhosts/example.com_conf
Template that is copied.
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/vhosts/DOMAIN.conf
Virtual host that is written.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
